{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":3,"delta":{"type":"input_json_delta","partial_json":"c/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md"}},"session_id":"77af4b8d-fd36-430f-8eea-47bd404bad4c","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"a4fd41ee-1d63-475a-a83b-d0a6cbd63fa5"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GiVtLqABvhqfqwupkLkzf8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\"command\":\"epic-review\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"blocked\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"result\":{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"canonicalReview\":{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"reviewerLabels\":[\"epic-reviewer-1\",\"epic-reviewer-2\"],\"reconciliationSummary\":\"Both reviewers agree on nearly the whole epic: gates green (independently re-run by this canonical pass: pnpm verify-all exit 0, 366/366 tests, 44 files, process suite ran), composition discipline structural, read-only enforced at two layers, approved rulings (011 Story 3 loadCost/sourceState, 011 Story 4 threadId-normalized file equality, 023 strict-read-purity) implemented exactly, no fake or placeholder production paths. The one material disagreement is the health queue section. epic-reviewer-1 treated the listQueuedWork→report-entry-join substitution as a surface-respecting design drift ('arguably stronger for AC-4.5', observation only); epic-reviewer-2 blocked on it with a reproduced divergence (queued:5 vs 4 live work items). Independent verification confirms reviewer-2 on every link: health.ts:92-95 increments queue once per FormReportEntry with a queue join and never calls listQueuedWork; turns/internal/forms.ts:266,296 ('Both turn forms map to the one turn_derivation kind') makes one live turn_derivation work item join onto two form rows (turn_rendering + lower_band_projection); and the shipped test inspect-health.test.ts:174 itself pins queued:5 for the post-edit cascade whose owners' queue detail holds exactly 4 work items (prompt_smoothing, turn_derivation, chunk_summary_brief, chunk_summary_detailed) — so the divergence is pinned by the default suite, not edge-case-only. Epic AC-4.5's governing text ('queued and claimed work counts from the owners' queue detail') and the epic NFR ('where a report describes another surface's output ... equality is contractual') are not satisfied as written, no ruling covers the substitution (impl-log rulings 011/011/023 cover other contracts), and the tech design is internally ambiguous (Flow 4 names listQueuedWork as an input yet says 'queue = counts from the live-item joins'). Per the conservative rule, the blocker is retained, not downgraded: EV-04-001 stands as the single blocking finding (absorbing the health half of E04-ER1-002), with human-ruling scope because both fix paths alter a spec'd contract — either count work items from queue detail (breaking the queued+claimed = pending+retrying identity TC-4.1 leans on) or ratify form-entry semantics and amend AC-4.5/tech-design wording. Reviewer-1's doc-lag finding (E04-ER1-001) and reviewer-2's (EV-04-002) are the same issue and are merged into one minor finding, fully verified against epic.md:149/156, test-plan.md:38, coverage.md:48, tech-design.md:94 (DD-4 stored-sum wording vs view-report.ts:67 measured tokens), and stories/03-view-contents-report.md ('Spec Deviations: None' despite approved ruling-011). Reviewer-1's remaining observations (overview boundary via pull.meta because ViewStatus at shared/view.ts:128-135 exposes no boundaryPosition; stale stub-era comment at cli/index.ts:473-475) were independently confirmed and retained as non-blocking. No reviewer finding was discarded as unsupported.\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Story handoffs completed as tracked: the Story 2 interim view-summary source (pull().meta) was swapped to threadView.describe in Story 3 (overview.ts:121-131), and the Story 2 inspect.view stub was replaced by the real composeViewReport — receipt-tracked risks are closed in code, not just in the log.\",\"Shared vocabulary discipline holds: report shapes live in src/shared/inspect.ts and Story 3 consumes them without redefinition; messages.show reuses the owner's report(messageId) read (DD-2); one lifecycle script (test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts) drives all four TC-5 legs including the process-suite leg (DD-8).\",\"Confirmed cross-story semantic drift (the blocker): Flow 4's health.queue counts form-report entries with live queue joins, while Epic 02's queue-detail surfaces (listQueuedWork) count work items — a turn_derivation work item owning both turn forms is counted twice by health (EV-04-001).\",\"Cumulative test baseline never regressed across the four accepted stories (290 → 300 → 313 → 320 → 328 default tests); epic gate re-run for this canonical review: 366/366 tests across 44 files with the process suite executed.\",\"All four story receipts in team-impl-log.md show accepted status with verifier PASS and disposition of every finding; approved rulings are reflected accurately in shipped code — but the health-queue substitution was never the subject of any ruling.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"Composition discipline is structural: domains/inspect imports only other domains' index surfaces, check-boundaries.mjs carries the inspect allowlist plus the Epic 04 source check rejecting raw storage access from domains/inspect/**, and the gate runs it; the domain-graph addition is acyclic as designed.\",\"Read-only is enforced at two layers per DD-6: every new operation runs under touch suppression, and tests assert absence-of-delta over observable state including the Story 3 storedView field added to the snapshot.\",\"Tech design Flow 4 is internally ambiguous and the ambiguity was resolved silently in code: the flow names listQueuedWork (both owners) as a health input and the External Contracts table lists it as 'Used by ... health', yet the same paragraph says 'queue = queued/claimed counts from the live-item joins'. health.ts implemented the latter reading and never calls listQueuedWork; no design deviation was recorded and no ruling was sought (feeds EV-04-001).\",\"DD-5 ('overview takes boundary via status') is impossible as written: ViewStatus (src/shared/view.ts:128-135) exposes no boundaryPosition, so overview.ts:121-128 reads it from pull.meta — the only surface exposing it — at the cost of a full pull render per overview call. Surface-respecting, but unrecorded in the tech design (E04-ER1-002).\",\"Approved public-contract deviations are implemented exactly as ruled: loadCost.bandTokens measured from pull-served band messages (view-report.ts:67, ruling-011 Story 3), sourceState/meta nullable for never-compacted threads, threadId-normalized materialized-file equality with literal pull-output hash equality (lifecycle.test.ts:17-22, ruling-011 Story 4).\",\"Error model and CLI conventions inherited cleanly: one additive caller_error code (invalid_bounds, approved); CLI commands are thin argv-to-SDK wrappers so parity including refusals is structural.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"22 of 23 ACs and 16 of 17 TCs are implemented, traceable, and green: test describe blocks name their TC/AC pairs across inspect-overview, inspect-view, messages-read, inspect-health, lifecycle, and cli-process-inspect test files; epic gate re-run by this canonical review passed (pnpm verify-all, exit 0, 366/366 tests, 44 files, process suite ran).\",\"AC-4.5 is not conclusively covered as written: TC-4.1's and TC-4.3's shipped assertions (inspect-health.test.ts:63, :174) pin the form-entry semantics — queue equals pending+retrying entry counts — not 'work counts from the owners' queue detail'; on the post-edit cascade the pinned value (queued:5) diverges from the queue-detail work-item count (4).\",\"AC-5.3/AC-5.4 ship as threadId-normalized file equality per approved Story 4 ruling-011 (the thread id is the design's one random value; everything else byte-identical, Date frozen so pull-output hash equality stays literal); the relaxation is principled and recorded in the story spec, but epic-level docs still carry the superseded literal wording (EV-04-002).\",\"Zero-provider NFR verified structurally for the whole epic: inspect/list/show/describe run green under a throwing provider; the lifecycle's only provider is the registry's deterministic one.\",\"Closeout items still owed: the M3/M4 quality-half transfer to the inference epic must be recorded, and the sanctioned PRD/tech-arch search-deferral backfill exists only as uncommitted working-tree changes (see unresolvedItems).\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No fake adapters, shims, or placeholder execution paths remain on any production path: the not_implemented code survives only as vocabulary in shared/errors.ts, the Story 2 inspect.view stub was replaced by the real implementation in Story 3, and the lifecycle exercise runs the real production SDK through the production registry.\",\"Provider posture is honest by construction: the registry contains exactly one provider (deterministic — the spec'd v1 state), there is no default provider, and the CLI fails with provider_not_configured rather than silently substituting.\",\"Confirmed material production-path issue (EV-04-001): inspect.health's queue section reports per-form-entry counts, not live work-item counts; on the standard mutation-in-flight cascade it reports queued:5 while the owners' listQueuedWork surfaces hold 4 work items, so the report disagrees with the queue-detail surface an operator would drill into.\",\"Cosmetic only: src/cli/index.ts:473-475 still carries the stub-era comment describing 'inspect view' as not-implemented; the route is real and in the help text (E04-ER1-003).\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-04-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Health queue counts are form-entry counts, not the queue-detail work counts AC-4.5 specifies — confirmed divergence, pinned by the shipped tests\",\"evidence\":\"Epic AC-4.5 requires 'queued and claimed work counts from the owners' queue detail'; tech-design Flow 4 and its External Contracts table name listQueuedWork (both owners) as a health input. composeHealth (src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts:40-106) reads only messages.report + turns.report and increments queue once per FormReportEntry carrying a queue join (lines 89-95); it never calls listQueuedWork. The divergence is structural: the turns report join maps BOTH turn forms (turn_rendering, lower_band_projection) to the one turn_derivation work-item kind (src/domains/turns/internal/forms.ts:266,294-301), so one live turn-derivation item is counted twice. The shipped default suite pins the divergent value: inspect-health.test.ts:174 asserts queue {queued:5, claimed:0} for the post-edit cascade whose owners' queue detail holds exactly 4 work items (prompt_smoothing, turn_derivation, chunk_summary_brief, chunk_summary_detailed) — matching epic-reviewer-2's independent reproduction. This violates AC-4.5's source clause and the epic NFR 'where a report describes another surface's output ... equality is contractual', and no approved ruling covers the substitution. Human ruling required because both fix paths alter spec'd contract text: counting work items from queue detail breaks the queued+claimed = pending+retrying identity the current TC-4.1 assertion leans on, while ratifying form-entry semantics requires amending AC-4.5, tech-design Flow 4/External Contracts, and the test-plan TC-4.1 spine.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/inspect-health.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/lifecycle.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.5\",\"TC-4.1\",\"tech-design Flow 4: Health\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-04-002\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Epic-level artifacts not updated for approved ruling-011 deviations (threadId-normalized file equality; measured loadCost.bandTokens)\",\"evidence\":\"Merged from E04-ER1-001 and EV-04-002; all citations verified. Story 4 ruling-011 (approved) relaxed materialized-file equality to substitute only the random thread id (implemented in lifecycle.test.ts:17-22 and the file-equality assertions), but epic.md AC-5.3/TC-5.2 (lines 149, 156), test-plan.md TC-5.2 (line 38), and stories/coverage.md (line 48) still say byte-identical/hash-equal with no qualifier. Story 3 ruling-011 (approved) made loadCost.bandTokens measured from pull-served band messages (view-report.ts:67), but tech-design.md DD-4 (line 94) still says 'sum of stored band counts', and stories/03-view-contents-report.md's Spec Deviations section still says 'None.' despite that approved public-contract deviation. Code and tests implement the ruled contracts correctly; only the docs lag.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/coverage.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/03-view-contents-report.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.3\",\"AC-2.5\",\"AC-5.3\",\"AC-5.4\",\"TC-5.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E04-ER1-002\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Tech design DD-5 not backfilled: overview reads the visibility boundary from pull.meta because ViewStatus exposes no boundaryPosition\",\"evidence\":\"tech-design.md DD-5 says overview composes boundary/zone 'via status', but ViewStatus (src/shared/view.ts:128-135) has no boundaryPosition field — overview.ts:121-128 reads it from pull.meta, the only surface exposing it, at the cost of a full pull render per overview call. Surface-respecting and AC-1.1-satisfying, but unrecorded as a design deviation. (The health half of the original finding — the listQueuedWork substitution — is escalated into blocking finding EV-04-001 and not duplicated here.)\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/overview.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E04-ER1-003\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Stale stub-era comment on the 'inspect view' CLI route\",\"evidence\":\"src/cli/index.ts:473-475 still says the route 'returns the structured not-implemented result; Story 3 makes it real (and adds it to the help text)' — Story 3 landed, runInspectView is the real implementation, and the command is in the help text. Comment is false; code is correct.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/cli/index.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Human ruling required for EV-04-001: decide whether HealthReport.queue counts live work items (per epic AC-4.5's 'work counts from the owners' queue detail' — requires reworking health.ts to consume listQueuedWork and re-stating TC-4.1's consistency clause, since queued+claimed would no longer equal pending+retrying when a turn derivation is in flight) or pending/retrying form entries (per the shipped implementation and tests — requires amending AC-4.5, tech-design Flow 4 and External Contracts, and the test-plan TC-4.1 spine to ratify the deviation).\",\"Uncommitted working-tree changes carry the sanctioned PRD AC-4.3 search-deferral backfill (packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/00-prd.md, 01-tech-arch.md) plus impl-log bookkeeping — epic-mandated doc changes that must be committed as part of epic closeout.\",\"Epic closeout must record the M3/M4 quality-half transfer to the inference epic explicitly (epic.md Assumptions); not yet written — this review is upstream of that closeout step.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"},\"verifierResults\":[{\"resultId\":\"6b026f0b-72fd-4f16-88b6-28f3f56e2b90\",\"outcome\":\"pass\",\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"model\":\"claude-fable-5\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-reviewer-1\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Story 2 → Story 3 handoff completed as tracked: overview's interim view-summary source (pull().meta, Story 2 approved deviation) was swapped to threadView.describe in Story 3 (overview.ts), and the Story 2 inspect.view stub was replaced with the real composeViewReport. The receipt-tracked risk is closed in code, not just in the log.\",\"Shared vocabulary discipline holds across stories: report shapes live in src/shared/inspect.ts (Story 2) and Story 3 consumes them without redefinition; messages.show reuses the owner's reportMessageForms read (DD-2) rather than new join machinery; the lifecycle fixture (test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts) is one script driven by all four TC-5 legs including the process-suite leg (DD-8), so replay/teardown/CLI runs exercise the same sequence.\",\"The read-only delta helper (test/fixtures/read-only-delta.ts, Story 2) wraps Story 1's ops retroactively as the test plan required: inspect-overview/view/health tests use expectReadOnly, messages-read uses the same observableState snapshot directly, and the Story 3 storedView field was added to the snapshot so a forgotten view touch is caught even when pull meta would not show it.\",\"Cumulative baseline never regressed: 290 → 300 → 313 → 320 → 328 default tests across the four accepted stories; epic gate run for this review shows 366 tests / 44 files with the process suite included.\",\"All four story receipts in team-impl-log.md show accepted status with verifier PASS, impl-lead-run gates, and disposition of every finding (SV-01-001..005, SV-03-001, SV-04-001); approved rulings (023 strict-read-purity, 011 Story 3 loadCost/sourceState, 011 Story 4 threadId-normalized file equality) are all reflected accurately in the shipped code.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"Composition discipline is structural, not aspirational: domains/inspect imports only the five other domains' index surfaces (verified in source), check-boundaries.mjs carries the inspect dependency allowlist plus the Epic 04 source check rejecting raw storage access from domains/inspect/** (scripts/check-boundaries.mjs:77-115), and the gate runs it. The domain graph addition is acyclic as designed.\",\"Read-only is enforced at two layers as DD-6 demanded: every new operation (inspect.overview/view/health, threadView.describe, messages.listMessages/show) runs under runWithThreadTouchSuppressed so a background scheduler can never hang a catch-up drain off a read, and tests assert absence-of-delta over observable state including raw derived_form rows.\",\"Minor drift from tech-design mechanics, surface-respecting in both cases: (1) DD-5 says overview takes boundary 'via status' but ViewStatus does not expose boundaryPosition — the implementation reads it from pull.meta (overview.ts:125-129, commented), which is the only surface exposing it; side effect is that every overview call performs a full pull render. (2) Tech design Flow 4 names listQueuedWork as a health input, but health.ts derives queue counts from the report entries' queue joins instead — consistent-by-construction with the same report's state counts, which is arguably stronger for AC-4.5, but the tech design was not updated to record either substitution.\",\"Approved public-contract deviations are implemented exactly as ruled: loadCost.bandTokens measured from pull-served band messages rather than stored sums (ruling-011 Story 3; AC-2.3's equality is the governing contract and the shared/inspect.ts comment documents why stored sums structurally cannot match), and sourceState/meta nullable for never-compacted threads.\",\"Error model and CLI conventions inherited cleanly: one additive caller_error code (invalid_bounds, Story 1 approved ruling, Epic 03 precedent), no other additions; CLI commands are thin argv-to-SDK wrappers with semantic validation kept in the SDK so parity including refusals is structural (cli/inspect.ts, cli/messages-read.ts).\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"All 23 ACs and 17 TCs are implemented and traceable: test describe blocks name their TC/AC pairs explicitly across inspect-overview.test.ts (TC-1.1–1.3), inspect-view.test.ts (TC-2.1–2.3 + describe purity legs), messages-read.test.ts (TC-3.1–3.3 + three architecture-risk suites), inspect-health.test.ts (TC-4.1–4.3 + provider-free leg), lifecycle.test.ts (TC-5.1–5.3 with all four AC-5.2 checkpoint assertions including the receipt-vs-health cross-check), and cli-process-inspect.test.ts (TC-3.4, TC-5.4, process suite).\",\"AC-5.3/AC-5.4 materialized-file equality ships as threadId-normalized equality per approved Story 4 ruling-011: thread id is the design's one random value, the test substitutes only it and requires every other byte identical, with Date frozen so pull-output hash equality stays literal with zero normalization. The relaxation is principled, documented in the test header, and recorded in the story spec.\",\"Zero-provider NFR is verified structurally for the whole epic: inspect/list/show/describe run green under a throwing provider, and the lifecycle's only provider is the registry's deterministic one (zero network, zero real-provider calls — AC-5.1).\",\"Epic gate run by this reviewer: pnpm verify-all PASS, exit 0, 366/366 tests across 44 files with the process suite executed (LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 is baked into verify-all), build/typecheck/lint/boundaries all green.\",\"Closeout items still owed per the epic's own assumptions: the M3/M4 quality-half transfer to the inference epic must be recorded at closeout, and the search-deferral PRD/tech-arch backfill exists but is uncommitted (see unresolvedItems).\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No fake adapters, shims, or placeholder execution paths remain on any production path. Grep for stub/placeholder/not-implemented across src/ finds only SQL parameter placeholders, comments, and the not_implemented code's vocabulary entry in shared/errors.ts — no operation returns it anymore; the Story 2 inspect.view stub was replaced by the real implementation in Story 3.\",\"Provider posture is honest by construction: the registry (src/providers/registry.ts) contains exactly one provider — deterministic — which is the spec'd v1 state (real inference is explicitly next-PRD scope, carried in the epic's Out of Scope). There is no default provider: the CLI resolves only an explicitly named provider (--provider/LHC_PROVIDER) and fails with provider_not_configured rather than silently substituting the deterministic one.\",\"The lifecycle exercise runs the real production SDK (createSdk) in background mode through the production registry's deterministic provider and the real drainSettled awaitable — no test-only seams in the sequence itself; the one test-only control is freezing Date in the test file, which is outside the production path.\",\"Stale comment, cosmetic only: src/cli/index.ts:473-475 still describes 'inspect view' as a not-implemented stub that 'Story 3 makes real' — Story 3 landed, the route is real, and the command is in the help text. The comment is now false; the code is correct.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"E04-ER1-001\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Epic-level docs still carry literal 'byte-identical' phrasing superseded by approved ruling-011 (threadId-normalized file equality)\",\"evidence\":\"epic.md AC-5.3/TC-5.2 (lines 149, 156-157), test-plan.md TC-5.2 (line 38), and coverage.md line 48 state byte-identical materialized-file equality; Story 4 ruling-011 (approved, recorded in team-impl-log.md and stories/04-lifecycle-exercise.md) relaxed file equality to substitute the one random thread id, with pull-output hash equality remaining literal. The impl log itself flags this for epic-review awareness. The shipped test (lifecycle.test.ts:17-22, 97-104) implements the ruled contract correctly; only the epic-level docs lag.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/coverage.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-5.3\",\"AC-5.4\",\"TC-5.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E04-ER1-002\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Tech design not backfilled for two surface-respecting mechanism substitutions (overview boundary via pull.meta; health queue via report join)\",\"evidence\":\"tech-design.md DD-5 says overview takes boundary/zone 'via status', but ViewStatus (src/shared/view.ts:128-135) exposes no boundaryPosition — overview.ts:125-129 reads it from pull.meta, the only surface that exposes it, at the cost of a full pull render per overview call. Tech-design Flow 4 and the System View name listQueuedWork as a health input, but health.ts derives queue counts from FormReportEntry queue joins (consistent-by-construction with the same report's state counts). Both substitutions stay on surfaces and satisfy their ACs; neither is recorded as a design deviation.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/overview.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"AC-4.5\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E04-ER1-003\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Stale stub-era comment on the 'inspect view' CLI route\",\"evidence\":\"src/cli/index.ts:473-475 says the route is 'routed ahead of its story so the CLI mirrors the SDK surface: the stub returns the structured not-implemented result; Story 3 makes it real (and adds it to the help text)' — Story 3 landed; runInspectView is the real implementation and the command appears in the help text (line 72). Comment is false, code is correct.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/cli/index.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Uncommitted working-tree changes carry the sanctioned PRD AC-4.3 search-deferral backfill (packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/00-prd.md, 01-tech-arch.md) plus impl-log state bookkeeping — these are epic-mandated doc changes (epic.md Out of Scope: 'backfilled with this epic') and should be committed as part of epic closeout.\",\"Epic closeout must record the M3/M4 quality-half transfer to the inference epic explicitly (epic.md Assumptions: 'Closeout records this explicitly') — not yet written; this review is upstream of that closeout step.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"},{\"resultId\":\"7037aa32-e09d-4f0a-b954-6917da95a54b\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.5\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-reviewer-2\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Stories 1-4 are wired through the SDK and CLI and the configured gates pass: `pnpm verify` passed with 328 tests and `pnpm verify-all` passed with 366 tests / 44 files, including the process suite.\",\"Flow 4 has unresolved cross-story semantic drift: `inspect.health.queue` reports one queued/claimed count per pending form report entry, while the epic and tech design describe queued/claimed work counts from owner queue detail. A turn-derivation work item that owns two forms is counted twice by health.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"`domains/inspect/**` imports owner surfaces only; `check-boundaries` passed and the inspect source check found no raw SQL/table access in inspect.\",\"`inspect.view` and lifecycle determinism intentionally follow approved rulings, but the epic-level artifacts still contain older wording for materialized-file byte identity and the tech design still says `loadCost.bandTokens` is the stored band-count sum.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Most epic ACs have direct default/process suite coverage across `messages-read`, `inspect-overview`, `inspect-health`, `inspect-view`, `lifecycle`, and `cli-process-inspect`.\",\"AC-4.5 is not conclusively covered because the tests assert consistency with pending form-entry counts, not queue-detail work-item counts.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No material fake adapter, shim, placeholder, or non-real production execution path was found in the audited SDK/CLI inspect, message-read, thread-view, and lifecycle paths.\",\"Material production-path issue: `inspect.health` derives queue counts from `FormReportEntry.queue` per form entry and does not count live queue work rows; on a mutation-in-flight production fixture it returned `{queued:5, claimed:0}` while owner `listQueuedWork` surfaces showed four live work items.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-04-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Health queue counts do not match queue-detail work counts\",\"evidence\":\"Epic AC-4.5 requires queued and claimed work counts from owner queue detail; tech-design Flow 4 says `health` composes `messages.report` + `turns.report` + `listQueuedWork` both owners. In `src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts:40-105`, `composeHealth` only reads `messages.report` and `turns.report`, then increments `queue` once for every report entry with `entry.queue` at lines 89-95. In an ad hoc mutation-in-flight fixture, `inspect.health` returned `healthQueue:{queued:5,claimed:0}` while `messages.listQueuedWork` + `turns.listQueuedWork` returned four work item ids: `w-m5-prompt_smoothing-v2`, `w-t2-turn_derivation-v2`, `w-c1-chunk_summary_brief-v2`, `w-c1-chunk_summary_detailed-v2`.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/inspect-health.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/lifecycle.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.5\",\"TC-4.1\",\"tech-design Flow 4: Health\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-04-002\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Accepted deviation wording is not propagated through all epic-level artifacts\",\"evidence\":\"Story 4 and ruling-011 accept materialized-file equality after substituting only the random threadId, and tests implement that in `test/lifecycle.test.ts:97-103` and `:282-302`. The epic and test plan still say materialized files are byte-identical without that qualifier at `epic.md:149-157` and `test-plan.md:38-39`. Story 3/ruling-011 accepts measured pull-served `loadCost.bandTokens` and nullable `sourceState`, while `tech-design.md:94` still says `loadCost.bandTokens` is the sum of stored band counts and `stories/03-view-contents-report.md:119-121` still says no deviations.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/03-view-contents-report.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/04-lifecycle-exercise.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.3\",\"AC-2.5\",\"AC-5.3\",\"AC-5.4\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Decide whether `HealthReport.queue` is intended to count live work items or pending/retrying form entries. The current implementation and tests use form-entry counts; the epic/tech-design wording points to queue-detail work counts.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/epic/001-epic-review.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-12T15:43:43.996Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-12T15:54:28.853Z\"}\n2\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"77af4b8d-fd36-430f-8eea-47bd404bad4c","uuid":"424e2f32-086e-4dfc-9d55-76643b377be1","timestamp":"2026-06-12T16:04:02.490Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/epic/001-epic-review.json","content":"{\"command\":\"epic-review\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"blocked\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"result\":{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"canonicalReview\":{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"reviewerLabels\":[\"epic-reviewer-1\",\"epic-reviewer-2\"],\"reconciliationSummary\":\"Both reviewers agree on nearly the whole epic: gates green (independently re-run by this canonical pass: pnpm verify-all exit 0, 366/366 tests, 44 files, process suite ran), composition discipline structural, read-only enforced at two layers, approved rulings (011 Story 3 loadCost/sourceState, 011 Story 4 threadId-normalized file equality, 023 strict-read-purity) implemented exactly, no fake or placeholder production paths. The one material disagreement is the health queue section. epic-reviewer-1 treated the listQueuedWork→report-entry-join substitution as a surface-respecting design drift ('arguably stronger for AC-4.5', observation only); epic-reviewer-2 blocked on it with a reproduced divergence (queued:5 vs 4 live work items). Independent verification confirms reviewer-2 on every link: health.ts:92-95 increments queue once per FormReportEntry with a queue join and never calls listQueuedWork; turns/internal/forms.ts:266,296 ('Both turn forms map to the one turn_derivation kind') makes one live turn_derivation work item join onto two form rows (turn_rendering + lower_band_projection); and the shipped test inspect-health.test.ts:174 itself pins queued:5 for the post-edit cascade whose owners' queue detail holds exactly 4 work items (prompt_smoothing, turn_derivation, chunk_summary_brief, chunk_summary_detailed) — so the divergence is pinned by the default suite, not edge-case-only. Epic AC-4.5's governing text ('queued and claimed work counts from the owners' queue detail') and the epic NFR ('where a report describes another surface's output ... equality is contractual') are not satisfied as written, no ruling covers the substitution (impl-log rulings 011/011/023 cover other contracts), and the tech design is internally ambiguous (Flow 4 names listQueuedWork as an input yet says 'queue = counts from the live-item joins'). Per the conservative rule, the blocker is retained, not downgraded: EV-04-001 stands as the single blocking finding (absorbing the health half of E04-ER1-002), with human-ruling scope because both fix paths alter a spec'd contract — either count work items from queue detail (breaking the queued+claimed = pending+retrying identity TC-4.1 leans on) or ratify form-entry semantics and amend AC-4.5/tech-design wording. Reviewer-1's doc-lag finding (E04-ER1-001) and reviewer-2's (EV-04-002) are the same issue and are merged into one minor finding, fully verified against epic.md:149/156, test-plan.md:38, coverage.md:48, tech-design.md:94 (DD-4 stored-sum wording vs view-report.ts:67 measured tokens), and stories/03-view-contents-report.md ('Spec Deviations: None' despite approved ruling-011). Reviewer-1's remaining observations (overview boundary via pull.meta because ViewStatus at shared/view.ts:128-135 exposes no boundaryPosition; stale stub-era comment at cli/index.ts:473-475) were independently confirmed and retained as non-blocking. No reviewer finding was discarded as unsupported.\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Story handoffs completed as tracked: the Story 2 interim view-summary source (pull().meta) was swapped to threadView.describe in Story 3 (overview.ts:121-131), and the Story 2 inspect.view stub was replaced by the real composeViewReport — receipt-tracked risks are closed in code, not just in the log.\",\"Shared vocabulary discipline holds: report shapes live in src/shared/inspect.ts and Story 3 consumes them without redefinition; messages.show reuses the owner's report(messageId) read (DD-2); one lifecycle script (test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts) drives all four TC-5 legs including the process-suite leg (DD-8).\",\"Confirmed cross-story semantic drift (the blocker): Flow 4's health.queue counts form-report entries with live queue joins, while Epic 02's queue-detail surfaces (listQueuedWork) count work items — a turn_derivation work item owning both turn forms is counted twice by health (EV-04-001).\",\"Cumulative test baseline never regressed across the four accepted stories (290 → 300 → 313 → 320 → 328 default tests); epic gate re-run for this canonical review: 366/366 tests across 44 files with the process suite executed.\",\"All four story receipts in team-impl-log.md show accepted status with verifier PASS and disposition of every finding; approved rulings are reflected accurately in shipped code — but the health-queue substitution was never the subject of any ruling.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"Composition discipline is structural: domains/inspect imports only other domains' index surfaces, check-boundaries.mjs carries the inspect allowlist plus the Epic 04 source check rejecting raw storage access from domains/inspect/**, and the gate runs it; the domain-graph addition is acyclic as designed.\",\"Read-only is enforced at two layers per DD-6: every new operation runs under touch suppression, and tests assert absence-of-delta over observable state including the Story 3 storedView field added to the snapshot.\",\"Tech design Flow 4 is internally ambiguous and the ambiguity was resolved silently in code: the flow names listQueuedWork (both owners) as a health input and the External Contracts table lists it as 'Used by ... health', yet the same paragraph says 'queue = queued/claimed counts from the live-item joins'. health.ts implemented the latter reading and never calls listQueuedWork; no design deviation was recorded and no ruling was sought (feeds EV-04-001).\",\"DD-5 ('overview takes boundary via status') is impossible as written: ViewStatus (src/shared/view.ts:128-135) exposes no boundaryPosition, so overview.ts:121-128 reads it from pull.meta — the only surface exposing it — at the cost of a full pull render per overview call. Surface-respecting, but unrecorded in the tech design (E04-ER1-002).\",\"Approved public-contract deviations are implemented exactly as ruled: loadCost.bandTokens measured from pull-served band messages (view-report.ts:67, ruling-011 Story 3), sourceState/meta nullable for never-compacted threads, threadId-normalized materialized-file equality with literal pull-output hash equality (lifecycle.test.ts:17-22, ruling-011 Story 4).\",\"Error model and CLI conventions inherited cleanly: one additive caller_error code (invalid_bounds, approved); CLI commands are thin argv-to-SDK wrappers so parity including refusals is structural.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"22 of 23 ACs and 16 of 17 TCs are implemented, traceable, and green: test describe blocks name their TC/AC pairs across inspect-overview, inspect-view, messages-read, inspect-health, lifecycle, and cli-process-inspect test files; epic gate re-run by this canonical review passed (pnpm verify-all, exit 0, 366/366 tests, 44 files, process suite ran).\",\"AC-4.5 is not conclusively covered as written: TC-4.1's and TC-4.3's shipped assertions (inspect-health.test.ts:63, :174) pin the form-entry semantics — queue equals pending+retrying entry counts — not 'work counts from the owners' queue detail'; on the post-edit cascade the pinned value (queued:5) diverges from the queue-detail work-item count (4).\",\"AC-5.3/AC-5.4 ship as threadId-normalized file equality per approved Story 4 ruling-011 (the thread id is the design's one random value; everything else byte-identical, Date frozen so pull-output hash equality stays literal); the relaxation is principled and recorded in the story spec, but epic-level docs still carry the superseded literal wording (EV-04-002).\",\"Zero-provider NFR verified structurally for the whole epic: inspect/list/show/describe run green under a throwing provider; the lifecycle's only provider is the registry's deterministic one.\",\"Closeout items still owed: the M3/M4 quality-half transfer to the inference epic must be recorded, and the sanctioned PRD/tech-arch search-deferral backfill exists only as uncommitted working-tree changes (see unresolvedItems).\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No fake adapters, shims, or placeholder execution paths remain on any production path: the not_implemented code survives only as vocabulary in shared/errors.ts, the Story 2 inspect.view stub was replaced by the real implementation in Story 3, and the lifecycle exercise runs the real production SDK through the production registry.\",\"Provider posture is honest by construction: the registry contains exactly one provider (deterministic — the spec'd v1 state), there is no default provider, and the CLI fails with provider_not_configured rather than silently substituting.\",\"Confirmed material production-path issue (EV-04-001): inspect.health's queue section reports per-form-entry counts, not live work-item counts; on the standard mutation-in-flight cascade it reports queued:5 while the owners' listQueuedWork surfaces hold 4 work items, so the report disagrees with the queue-detail surface an operator would drill into.\",\"Cosmetic only: src/cli/index.ts:473-475 still carries the stub-era comment describing 'inspect view' as not-implemented; the route is real and in the help text (E04-ER1-003).\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-04-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Health queue counts are form-entry counts, not the queue-detail work counts AC-4.5 specifies — confirmed divergence, pinned by the shipped tests\",\"evidence\":\"Epic AC-4.5 requires 'queued and claimed work counts from the owners' queue detail'; tech-design Flow 4 and its External Contracts table name listQueuedWork (both owners) as a health input. composeHealth (src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts:40-106) reads only messages.report + turns.report and increments queue once per FormReportEntry carrying a queue join (lines 89-95); it never calls listQueuedWork. The divergence is structural: the turns report join maps BOTH turn forms (turn_rendering, lower_band_projection) to the one turn_derivation work-item kind (src/domains/turns/internal/forms.ts:266,294-301), so one live turn-derivation item is counted twice. The shipped default suite pins the divergent value: inspect-health.test.ts:174 asserts queue {queued:5, claimed:0} for the post-edit cascade whose owners' queue detail holds exactly 4 work items (prompt_smoothing, turn_derivation, chunk_summary_brief, chunk_summary_detailed) — matching epic-reviewer-2's independent reproduction. This violates AC-4.5's source clause and the epic NFR 'where a report describes another surface's output ... equality is contractual', and no approved ruling covers the substitution. Human ruling required because both fix paths alter spec'd contract text: counting work items from queue detail breaks the queued+claimed = pending+retrying identity the current TC-4.1 assertion leans on, while ratifying form-entry semantics requires amending AC-4.5, tech-design Flow 4/External Contracts, and the test-plan TC-4.1 spine.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/inspect-health.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/lifecycle.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.5\",\"TC-4.1\",\"tech-design Flow 4: Health\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-04-002\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Epic-level artifacts not updated for approved ruling-011 deviations (threadId-normalized file equality; measured loadCost.bandTokens)\",\"evidence\":\"Merged from E04-ER1-001 and EV-04-002; all citations verified. Story 4 ruling-011 (approved) relaxed materialized-file equality to substitute only the random thread id (implemented in lifecycle.test.ts:17-22 and the file-equality assertions), but epic.md AC-5.3/TC-5.2 (lines 149, 156), test-plan.md TC-5.2 (line 38), and stories/coverage.md (line 48) still say byte-identical/hash-equal with no qualifier. Story 3 ruling-011 (approved) made loadCost.bandTokens measured from pull-served band messages (view-report.ts:67), but tech-design.md DD-4 (line 94) still says 'sum of stored band counts', and stories/03-view-contents-report.md's Spec Deviations section still says 'None.' despite that approved public-contract deviation. Code and tests implement the ruled contracts correctly; only the docs lag.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/coverage.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/03-view-contents-report.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.3\",\"AC-2.5\",\"AC-5.3\",\"AC-5.4\",\"TC-5.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E04-ER1-002\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Tech design DD-5 not backfilled: overview reads the visibility boundary from pull.meta because ViewStatus exposes no boundaryPosition\",\"evidence\":\"tech-design.md DD-5 says overview composes boundary/zone 'via status', but ViewStatus (src/shared/view.ts:128-135) has no boundaryPosition field — overview.ts:121-128 reads it from pull.meta, the only surface exposing it, at the cost of a full pull render per overview call. Surface-respecting and AC-1.1-satisfying, but unrecorded as a design deviation. (The health half of the original finding — the listQueuedWork substitution — is escalated into blocking finding EV-04-001 and not duplicated here.)\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/overview.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E04-ER1-003\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Stale stub-era comment on the 'inspect view' CLI route\",\"evidence\":\"src/cli/index.ts:473-475 still says the route 'returns the structured not-implemented result; Story 3 makes it real (and adds it to the help text)' — Story 3 landed, runInspectView is the real implementation, and the command is in the help text. Comment is false; code is correct.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/cli/index.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Human ruling required for EV-04-001: decide whether HealthReport.queue counts live work items (per epic AC-4.5's 'work counts from the owners' queue detail' — requires reworking health.ts to consume listQueuedWork and re-stating TC-4.1's consistency clause, since queued+claimed would no longer equal pending+retrying when a turn derivation is in flight) or pending/retrying form entries (per the shipped implementation and tests — requires amending AC-4.5, tech-design Flow 4 and External Contracts, and the test-plan TC-4.1 spine to ratify the deviation).\",\"Uncommitted working-tree changes carry the sanctioned PRD AC-4.3 search-deferral backfill (packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/00-prd.md, 01-tech-arch.md) plus impl-log bookkeeping — epic-mandated doc changes that must be committed as part of epic closeout.\",\"Epic closeout must record the M3/M4 quality-half transfer to the inference epic explicitly (epic.md Assumptions); not yet written — this review is upstream of that closeout step.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"},\"verifierResults\":[{\"resultId\":\"6b026f0b-72fd-4f16-88b6-28f3f56e2b90\",\"outcome\":\"pass\",\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"model\":\"claude-fable-5\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-reviewer-1\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Story 2 → Story 3 handoff completed as tracked: overview's interim view-summary source (pull().meta, Story 2 approved deviation) was swapped to threadView.describe in Story 3 (overview.ts), and the Story 2 inspect.view stub was replaced with the real composeViewReport. The receipt-tracked risk is closed in code, not just in the log.\",\"Shared vocabulary discipline holds across stories: report shapes live in src/shared/inspect.ts (Story 2) and Story 3 consumes them without redefinition; messages.show reuses the owner's reportMessageForms read (DD-2) rather than new join machinery; the lifecycle fixture (test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts) is one script driven by all four TC-5 legs including the process-suite leg (DD-8), so replay/teardown/CLI runs exercise the same sequence.\",\"The read-only delta helper (test/fixtures/read-only-delta.ts, Story 2) wraps Story 1's ops retroactively as the test plan required: inspect-overview/view/health tests use expectReadOnly, messages-read uses the same observableState snapshot directly, and the Story 3 storedView field was added to the snapshot so a forgotten view touch is caught even when pull meta would not show it.\",\"Cumulative baseline never regressed: 290 → 300 → 313 → 320 → 328 default tests across the four accepted stories; epic gate run for this review shows 366 tests / 44 files with the process suite included.\",\"All four story receipts in team-impl-log.md show accepted status with verifier PASS, impl-lead-run gates, and disposition of every finding (SV-01-001..005, SV-03-001, SV-04-001); approved rulings (023 strict-read-purity, 011 Story 3 loadCost/sourceState, 011 Story 4 threadId-normalized file equality) are all reflected accurately in the shipped code.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"Composition discipline is structural, not aspirational: domains/inspect imports only the five other domains' index surfaces (verified in source), check-boundaries.mjs carries the inspect dependency allowlist plus the Epic 04 source check rejecting raw storage access from domains/inspect/** (scripts/check-boundaries.mjs:77-115), and the gate runs it. The domain graph addition is acyclic as designed.\",\"Read-only is enforced at two layers as DD-6 demanded: every new operation (inspect.overview/view/health, threadView.describe, messages.listMessages/show) runs under runWithThreadTouchSuppressed so a background scheduler can never hang a catch-up drain off a read, and tests assert absence-of-delta over observable state including raw derived_form rows.\",\"Minor drift from tech-design mechanics, surface-respecting in both cases: (1) DD-5 says overview takes boundary 'via status' but ViewStatus does not expose boundaryPosition — the implementation reads it from pull.meta (overview.ts:125-129, commented), which is the only surface exposing it; side effect is that every overview call performs a full pull render. (2) Tech design Flow 4 names listQueuedWork as a health input, but health.ts derives queue counts from the report entries' queue joins instead — consistent-by-construction with the same report's state counts, which is arguably stronger for AC-4.5, but the tech design was not updated to record either substitution.\",\"Approved public-contract deviations are implemented exactly as ruled: loadCost.bandTokens measured from pull-served band messages rather than stored sums (ruling-011 Story 3; AC-2.3's equality is the governing contract and the shared/inspect.ts comment documents why stored sums structurally cannot match), and sourceState/meta nullable for never-compacted threads.\",\"Error model and CLI conventions inherited cleanly: one additive caller_error code (invalid_bounds, Story 1 approved ruling, Epic 03 precedent), no other additions; CLI commands are thin argv-to-SDK wrappers with semantic validation kept in the SDK so parity including refusals is structural (cli/inspect.ts, cli/messages-read.ts).\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"All 23 ACs and 17 TCs are implemented and traceable: test describe blocks name their TC/AC pairs explicitly across inspect-overview.test.ts (TC-1.1–1.3), inspect-view.test.ts (TC-2.1–2.3 + describe purity legs), messages-read.test.ts (TC-3.1–3.3 + three architecture-risk suites), inspect-health.test.ts (TC-4.1–4.3 + provider-free leg), lifecycle.test.ts (TC-5.1–5.3 with all four AC-5.2 checkpoint assertions including the receipt-vs-health cross-check), and cli-process-inspect.test.ts (TC-3.4, TC-5.4, process suite).\",\"AC-5.3/AC-5.4 materialized-file equality ships as threadId-normalized equality per approved Story 4 ruling-011: thread id is the design's one random value, the test substitutes only it and requires every other byte identical, with Date frozen so pull-output hash equality stays literal with zero normalization. The relaxation is principled, documented in the test header, and recorded in the story spec.\",\"Zero-provider NFR is verified structurally for the whole epic: inspect/list/show/describe run green under a throwing provider, and the lifecycle's only provider is the registry's deterministic one (zero network, zero real-provider calls — AC-5.1).\",\"Epic gate run by this reviewer: pnpm verify-all PASS, exit 0, 366/366 tests across 44 files with the process suite executed (LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 is baked into verify-all), build/typecheck/lint/boundaries all green.\",\"Closeout items still owed per the epic's own assumptions: the M3/M4 quality-half transfer to the inference epic must be recorded at closeout, and the search-deferral PRD/tech-arch backfill exists but is uncommitted (see unresolvedItems).\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No fake adapters, shims, or placeholder execution paths remain on any production path. Grep for stub/placeholder/not-implemented across src/ finds only SQL parameter placeholders, comments, and the not_implemented code's vocabulary entry in shared/errors.ts — no operation returns it anymore; the Story 2 inspect.view stub was replaced by the real implementation in Story 3.\",\"Provider posture is honest by construction: the registry (src/providers/registry.ts) contains exactly one provider — deterministic — which is the spec'd v1 state (real inference is explicitly next-PRD scope, carried in the epic's Out of Scope). There is no default provider: the CLI resolves only an explicitly named provider (--provider/LHC_PROVIDER) and fails with provider_not_configured rather than silently substituting the deterministic one.\",\"The lifecycle exercise runs the real production SDK (createSdk) in background mode through the production registry's deterministic provider and the real drainSettled awaitable — no test-only seams in the sequence itself; the one test-only control is freezing Date in the test file, which is outside the production path.\",\"Stale comment, cosmetic only: src/cli/index.ts:473-475 still describes 'inspect view' as a not-implemented stub that 'Story 3 makes real' — Story 3 landed, the route is real, and the command is in the help text. The comment is now false; the code is correct.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"E04-ER1-001\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Epic-level docs still carry literal 'byte-identical' phrasing superseded by approved ruling-011 (threadId-normalized file equality)\",\"evidence\":\"epic.md AC-5.3/TC-5.2 (lines 149, 156-157), test-plan.md TC-5.2 (line 38), and coverage.md line 48 state byte-identical materialized-file equality; Story 4 ruling-011 (approved, recorded in team-impl-log.md and stories/04-lifecycle-exercise.md) relaxed file equality to substitute the one random thread id, with pull-output hash equality remaining literal. The impl log itself flags this for epic-review awareness. The shipped test (lifecycle.test.ts:17-22, 97-104) implements the ruled contract correctly; only the epic-level docs lag.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/coverage.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-5.3\",\"AC-5.4\",\"TC-5.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E04-ER1-002\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Tech design not backfilled for two surface-respecting mechanism substitutions (overview boundary via pull.meta; health queue via report join)\",\"evidence\":\"tech-design.md DD-5 says overview takes boundary/zone 'via status', but ViewStatus (src/shared/view.ts:128-135) exposes no boundaryPosition — overview.ts:125-129 reads it from pull.meta, the only surface that exposes it, at the cost of a full pull render per overview call. Tech-design Flow 4 and the System View name listQueuedWork as a health input, but health.ts derives queue counts from FormReportEntry queue joins (consistent-by-construction with the same report's state counts). Both substitutions stay on surfaces and satisfy their ACs; neither is recorded as a design deviation.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/overview.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"AC-4.5\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E04-ER1-003\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Stale stub-era comment on the 'inspect view' CLI route\",\"evidence\":\"src/cli/index.ts:473-475 says the route is 'routed ahead of its story so the CLI mirrors the SDK surface: the stub returns the structured not-implemented result; Story 3 makes it real (and adds it to the help text)' — Story 3 landed; runInspectView is the real implementation and the command appears in the help text (line 72). Comment is false, code is correct.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/cli/index.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Uncommitted working-tree changes carry the sanctioned PRD AC-4.3 search-deferral backfill (packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/00-prd.md, 01-tech-arch.md) plus impl-log state bookkeeping — these are epic-mandated doc changes (epic.md Out of Scope: 'backfilled with this epic') and should be committed as part of epic closeout.\",\"Epic closeout must record the M3/M4 quality-half transfer to the inference epic explicitly (epic.md Assumptions: 'Closeout records this explicitly') — not yet written; this review is upstream of that closeout step.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"},{\"resultId\":\"7037aa32-e09d-4f0a-b954-6917da95a54b\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.5\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-reviewer-2\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Stories 1-4 are wired through the SDK and CLI and the configured gates pass: `pnpm verify` passed with 328 tests and `pnpm verify-all` passed with 366 tests / 44 files, including the process suite.\",\"Flow 4 has unresolved cross-story semantic drift: `inspect.health.queue` reports one queued/claimed count per pending form report entry, while the epic and tech design describe queued/claimed work counts from owner queue detail. A turn-derivation work item that owns two forms is counted twice by health.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"`domains/inspect/**` imports owner surfaces only; `check-boundaries` passed and the inspect source check found no raw SQL/table access in inspect.\",\"`inspect.view` and lifecycle determinism intentionally follow approved rulings, but the epic-level artifacts still contain older wording for materialized-file byte identity and the tech design still says `loadCost.bandTokens` is the stored band-count sum.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Most epic ACs have direct default/process suite coverage across `messages-read`, `inspect-overview`, `inspect-health`, `inspect-view`, `lifecycle`, and `cli-process-inspect`.\",\"AC-4.5 is not conclusively covered because the tests assert consistency with pending form-entry counts, not queue-detail work-item counts.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No material fake adapter, shim, placeholder, or non-real production execution path was found in the audited SDK/CLI inspect, message-read, thread-view, and lifecycle paths.\",\"Material production-path issue: `inspect.health` derives queue counts from `FormReportEntry.queue` per form entry and does not count live queue work rows; on a mutation-in-flight production fixture it returned `{queued:5, claimed:0}` while owner `listQueuedWork` surfaces showed four live work items.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-04-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Health queue counts do not match queue-detail work counts\",\"evidence\":\"Epic AC-4.5 requires queued and claimed work counts from owner queue detail; tech-design Flow 4 says `health` composes `messages.report` + `turns.report` + `listQueuedWork` both owners. In `src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts:40-105`, `composeHealth` only reads `messages.report` and `turns.report`, then increments `queue` once for every report entry with `entry.queue` at lines 89-95. In an ad hoc mutation-in-flight fixture, `inspect.health` returned `healthQueue:{queued:5,claimed:0}` while `messages.listQueuedWork` + `turns.listQueuedWork` returned four work item ids: `w-m5-prompt_smoothing-v2`, `w-t2-turn_derivation-v2`, `w-c1-chunk_summary_brief-v2`, `w-c1-chunk_summary_detailed-v2`.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/inspect-health.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/lifecycle.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.5\",\"TC-4.1\",\"tech-design Flow 4: Health\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-04-002\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Accepted deviation wording is not propagated through all epic-level artifacts\",\"evidence\":\"Story 4 and ruling-011 accept materialized-file equality after substituting only the random threadId, and tests implement that in `test/lifecycle.test.ts:97-103` and `:282-302`. The epic and test plan still say materialized files are byte-identical without that qualifier at `epic.md:149-157` and `test-plan.md:38-39`. Story 3/ruling-011 accepts measured pull-served `loadCost.bandTokens` and nullable `sourceState`, while `tech-design.md:94` still says `loadCost.bandTokens` is the sum of stored band counts and `stories/03-view-contents-report.md:119-121` still says no deviations.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/03-view-contents-report.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/04-lifecycle-exercise.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.3\",\"AC-2.5\",\"AC-5.3\",\"AC-5.4\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Decide whether `HealthReport.queue` is intended to count live work items or pending/retrying form entries. The current implementation and tests use form-entry counts; the epic/tech-design wording points to queue-detail work counts.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/epic/001-epic-review.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-12T15:43:43.996Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-12T15:54:28.853Z\"}\n","numLines":2,"startLine":1,"totalLines":2}}}
